    [
     1,
     "On 04/28/2016 04:00 PM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kais...@stud.sbg.ac.at</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; Variances:\r<br>&gt; EstimateStd.Err Z-value  P(&gt;|z|)\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "&gt;      v1 0.3500.1212.8980.004\r<br>&gt;      v2 0.4730.1213.9240.000\r<br>&gt;      etc.\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt; How can I extract these values from the object?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "You can&#39;t. The summary() function is for display only. If you need to \r<br>extract values, please use the parameterEstimates() function. This \r<br>returns a data.frame, which you can filter in the usual way.\r<br>\r<br>For example:\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>library(lavaan)\r<br>example(cfa)\r<br>\r<br># all rows with variances\r<br>PE[ PE$op == &quot;~~&quot; &amp; PE$lhs == PE$rhs, ]\r<br>\r<br># all variance estimates\r<br>PE[ PE$op == &quot;~~&quot; &amp; PE$lhs == PE$rhs, &quot;est&quot;]\r<br>\r<br># observed (residual) variances only:\r<br>PE[ PE$op == &quot;~~&quot; &amp; PE$lhs == PE$rhs &amp; PE$lhs %in% lavNames(PE, &quot;ov&quot;), \r<br>&quot;est&quot;]\r<br>\r<br># latent variances only:\r<br>PE[ PE$op == &quot;~~&quot; &amp; PE$lhs == PE$rhs &amp; PE$lhs %in% lavNames(PE, &quot;lv&quot;), \r<br>&quot;est&quot;]\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
